From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bitpony <bitpony@example.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8189fs: serialize SDIO bulk and IRQ via bus worker

Route the high-risk SDIO CMD53 bulk read/write paths and SDIO IRQ DPC
execution through a single driver-owned bus worker. The worker always takes
the existing driver SDIO mutex before claiming the MMC host, so TX, command
and deferred IRQ work no longer race the host claim path with mixed lock
ordering.

Keep the inner TX, RX, command, HISR and DPC logic unchanged. IRQ handling is
only deferred to the bus worker with a pending-bit dedupe; if the worker is
not available, the original direct IRQ handling path remains as fallback.

Add an independent watchdog timer around the bus worker's active operation.
If one SDIO bus operation remains stuck, the watchdog logs the owner and
operation metadata, marks the primary adapter surprise-removed after a longer
timeout, and fails queued bus requests so new work stops piling onto the
stalled SDIO host.

Signed-off-by: bitpony <bitpony@example.com>
